  "note": "Covers Confluence Cloud's in-app shortcuts (General/Content, Formatting, Table) and Whiteboards, as documented on the source page. 'Open shortcut help' is skipped: the vendor lists it as Ctrl+? / Ctrl+?, but '?' isn't an expressible key in the chord grammar (only '/' is), and the page is internally inconsistent about this binding elsewhere (Shift+? while viewing, Ctrl+/ or Cmd+/ while editing) - listing it would mean guessing. Autocomplete trigger characters (Emoji ':', Mention '@', Image/media '!', Link '[Link](http://a.com)', Macro '{') and the separate Markdown autoformatting table (**bold**, *italic*, # headings, list/quote/divider/action-item/decision triggers) are in-field text-entry triggers, not fixed shortcuts, and are excluded per the grammar. 'Redo' has two documented bindings (Ctrl+Y and Ctrl+Shift+Z / Cmd+Y and Cmd+Shift+Z); both are listed as separate actions. 'Insert table column' and 'Insert table row' each document two bindings (=/- and ]/[) with no stated before/after semantics, so both are listed as primary + alternate. 'Select table row' and 'Select table column' each document two directional arrow bindings and are split into left/right and up/down actions respectively. 'Nudge element', 'Big nudge element', and 'Move whiteboard' are documented generically as 'Arrow keys' / 'Shift + Arrow keys'; each is expanded into its four directional actions. 'Code' appears under both Block formatting (Ctrl+Shift+M / Cmd+Shift+M, a code block) and Text formatting (Ctrl+Shift+M / Opt+Shift+M, inline code); kept as two actions distinguished by context since the Mac binding differs.",
